    "summary": "`X509Ref::ocsp_responders` can produce a `&str` that is not valid UTF-8",
    "details": "`X509Ref::ocsp_responders` returns the OCSP responder URLs from a certificate's Authority Information Access extension as `OpensslString` values, which dereference to `str` without validating the bytes. OpenSSL does not require these IA5String values to be ASCII, so for a certificate with non-UTF-8 bytes in an OCSP access location, safe code ends up holding a `&str` that is not valid UTF-8, which is undefined behavior. Certificates often come from untrusted peers.\n\n`ocsp_responders` was added in 0.9.7. 0.10.79 checks each URL and returns an error if it is not valid UTF-8.",
