    "summary": "Buffer overflow in `MdCtxRef::digest_final`",
    "details": "`MdCtxRef::digest_final` passed the caller's output slice to OpenSSL's `EVP_DigestFinal` without checking its length. `EVP_DigestFinal` always writes the full digest (`EVP_MD_CTX_size` bytes), so an output slice shorter than the digest is overrun. With a stack buffer this usually corrupts the stack. The overflow is reachable from safe code.\n\n`MdCtxRef` was added in 0.10.39. 0.10.78 checks the slice length first and returns an error when the slice is too short for the digest.",
